From f05df18aa18bafb06e6aa43f42fe3506ddcedecf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:12:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(title_bar): keep the close snapshot's text, fill
 order and buffer locks

The adaptive fill was copied into the close snapshot after the title and the
symbols, so it painted over them for the whole animation. Copy it where the live
tree has it, directly above the palette rects, and copy the title shadow with the
title.

A scene buffer drops its CPU-side buffer once the renderer has uploaded the
texture, so copying the live nodes by their buffer field lost the title (and any
visible symbol) from every snapshot. Ask the label cache for the same title again
and re-rasterize a symbol whose buffer has been released.

Also:
- release the mirrored buffer when the fill is disabled, or the scene keeps the
  client's buffer locked and its wl_buffer.release never arrives;
- keep the bar position and the corner radii in the reshape key, so a title bar
  height or radius change does not leave the fill misplaced or wrongly rounded;
- apply the surface colour description on every commit, since a colour
  management change carries no buffer damage;
- scale the title and symbol contrast edge by the colour's alpha, so an
  invisible title or symbol leaves no ghost of itself.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/scene/ssd_frame.cpp                       | 165 +++++++++++++-----
 src/scene/ssd_frame.h                         |   5 +
 .../checks/render/title_bar_adaptive.sh       |  63 ++++++-
 3 files changed, 185 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/scene/ssd_frame.cpp b/src/scene/ssd_frame.cpp
index dd7df076..3a392a17 100644
--- a/src/scene/ssd_frame.cpp
+++ b/src/scene/ssd_frame.cpp
@@ -23,9 +23,17 @@ namespace umbriel {
       return a.x == b.x && a.y == b.y && a.width == b.width && a.height == b.height;
     }
 
-    // An adaptive bar carries any colour the window paints, so text and symbols keep a dark edge under them.
