From 4bc3f42e11bc54cb461625a1649ca499aeaa2a96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:58:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(title_bar): address the external review round

- The strip box now takes the minimum last, so a viewport that maps less than
  one buffer pixel onto the surface cannot invert std::clamp's bounds (which
  aborts under _GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS) or produce a negative source origin; the
  result is clamped into the buffer.
- Mirroring the client buffer made wlroots refuse in-place shm damage on every
  commit, rebuilding the whole window's texture and changing the client buffer
  address (defeating the per-commit guard). The mirror now marks its lock as
  ignorable through a new umbrielfx helper and drops the mark when it is
  replaced, cleared or the frame is destroyed.
- The close snapshot copies the button backgrounds above the fill, matching the
  live tree, and reuses the icon buffers the frame already locks.
- Damage is only consulted on the commit that produced it, and the fractional
  strip is rounded outward before it is intersected.
- The strip follows the window geometry, so client-drawn shadow margins stay
  out of the bar colour.
- A surface without a colour description is reset to sRGB instead of keeping a
  stale transfer function.
- The title buffer is held across the shadow lookup, which could evict it.

Pins: a unit case for the sub-pixel strip (aborts without the clamp fix), and a
close-animation assertion for the button backgrounds (fails with the old
stacking order).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
